    "question": {
      ":question/id": "22ae691a-d08d-5791-81cb-bb4355f013fe",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & -6 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-70 & 0 & 56 \\\\ 12 & 1 & -10 \\\\ 70 & 0 & -67\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{22}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & -6 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-6R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-70 & 0 & 56 \\\\ 12 & 1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & -6 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}+6R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-70 & 0 & 56 \\\\ 12 & 1 & -10 \\\\ 70 & 0 & -67\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-6R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}+6R_{2}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
