      ":question/id": "de15e910-46a6-5224-818e-71d62e2e2b77",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 17 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 12 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{31}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}+7R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 17 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}+R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 17 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 12 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}+7R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}+R_{3}$.",
